# Bug: a pub function is reported private when an imported module defines an
# operator arm and a pub function of the same name.
#
# Module `vec` declares an operator arm (`-` on vec3) and `pub fn unit`.
# Module `rng` imports `vec` and declares its own `pub fn unit`. Calling
# `rng/unit` from here should print 42.
#
# What it does, on the interpreter and in `kanso check` alike:
#   error[opacity]: `unit` is private to module `rng` — only pub names cross
#   an import
#
# Rename vec's `-` arm to an ordinary function (say `twice`) and the program
# prints 42, so the operator arm is what turns the lookup wrong.
import "./rng"

print "{rng/unit (rng/seeded 42)}"
